[' Here's a JavaScript function named `renderFooterScripts` that meets your requirements:

```javascript
class Script {
  constructor({ scriptId, scriptType, scriptCode, dependencies }) {
    this.scriptId = scriptId;
    this.scriptType = scriptType;
    this.scriptCode = scriptCode;
    this.dependencies = dependencies || [];
  }
}

function renderFooterScripts(scripts) {
  const scriptMap = new Map();
  scripts.forEach((script) => {
    if (!scriptMap.has(script.scriptId)) {
      scriptMap.set(script.scriptId, script);
    } else {
      const existingScript = scriptMap.get(script.scriptId);
      existingScript.dependencies.push(script);
    }
  });

  let html = '';

  scriptMap.forEach((script) => {
    if (script.dependencies.length > 0) {
      script.dependencies.sort((a, b) => a.scriptId - b.scriptId);
      const dependentScripts = script.dependencies.map(renderDependentScript).join('');
      html += `<script id="${script.scriptId}" type="${script.scriptType}" ${dependentScripts}>${script.scriptCode}</script>`;
    } else {
      html += `<script id="${script.scriptId}" type="${script.scriptType}">${script.scriptCode}</script>`;
    }
  });

  function renderDependentScript(script) {
    return script.scriptType === 'defer' ? ` defer src="./${script.scriptCode}"` : ` src="./${script.scriptCode}"`;
  }

  return html;
}
```

This code creates a Script class to represent each script object, and the renderFooterScripts function takes an array of these Script objects as input. The function sorts the scripts based on their `scriptId`, handles dependencies by adding them to the corresponding script in the map, and renders the scripts as HTML `<script>` tags with the correct order and attributes.

The function also includes a helper function renderDependentScript to generate the appropriate attributes for deferred scripts. The function returns the final HTML string containing all the `<script>` tags in the correct order.

To support dynamic updates, you can simply update the array of Script objects and call renderFooterScripts again when needed without re-rendering the entire page. To handle unpredictable script loading times, consider using async scripts for external sources or implementing a loading spinner for long-running scripts.']

[' Here's a JavaScript function for an AngularJS application that meets your requirements:

