[' Here's a Java function that implements the described task using a custom Union-Find data structure, handles null values, edge cases, and includes logging for performance analysis:

```java
import java.time.Instant;
import java.util.*;

class UnionFind {
    private Map<Integer, Node> nodes;

    public UnionFind(int size) {
        nodes = new HashMap<>();
        for (int i = 0; i < size; i++) {
            nodes.put(i, new Node(i));
        }
    }

    public int findSet(int x) {
        if (x != nodes.get(x).parent) {
            nodes.get(x).path++;
            nodes.put(x.parent, nodes.get(x));
            x = nodes.get(x).parent;
        }
        return x;
    }

    public void unionSets(int x, int y) {
        int rootX = findSet(x);
        int rootY = findSet(y);

        if (rootX != rootY) {
            if (nodes.get(rootX).size > nodes.get(rootY).size) {
                nodes.get(rootY).parent = rootX;
                nodes.get(rootX).size += nodes.get(rootY).size;
            } else {
                nodes.get(rootX).parent = rootY;
                nodes.get(rootY).size += nodes.get(rootX).size;
            }
        }
    }
}

class Node {
    int id;
    int parent;
    int size;
    int path;

    public Node(int id) {
        this.id = id;
        this.parent = id;
        this.size = 1;
        this.path = 0;
    }
}

class Transaction {
    int id;
    Instant timestamp;
    String location;
    String deviceType;

    public Transaction(int id, Instant timestamp, String location, String deviceType) {
        this.id = id;
        this.timestamp = timestamp;
        this.location = location == null ? "" : location;
        this.deviceType = deviceType == null ? "" : deviceType;
    }
}

public class TransactionProcessor {
    private UnionFind uf;
    private final Logger logger;

    public TransactionProcessor(int size, Logger logger) {
        this.uf = new UnionFind(size);
        this.logger = logger;
    }

    public void processTransactions(List<Transaction> transactions) {
        long startTime = System.currentTimeMillis();
        Map<Integer, Transaction> transactionMap = new HashMap<>();

        for (Transaction transaction : transactions) {
            transactionMap.putIfAbsent(transaction.id, transaction);
            int rootId = uf.findSet(transaction.id);

            if (!transactionMap.get(rootId).location.equals(transaction.location) ||
                    ChronoUnit.MILLIS.between(transactionMap.get(rootId).timestamp, transaction.timestamp) <= 1000) {
                uf.unionSets(rootId, transaction.id);
            }
        }

        long endTime = System.currentTimeMillis();
        logger.log("Processed " + transactions.size() + " transactions in " + (endTime - startTime) + " milliseconds.");
    }
}

public interface Logger {
    void log(String message);
}
```

This code defines a `UnionFind` data structure, a `Transaction` class to represent user transactions, and a `TransactionProcessor` class that processes the transactions. The `Logger` interface is used for logging performance information.

The `processTransactions()` function in the `TransactionProcessor` class identifies disjoint transaction pairs based on the transaction ID while considering location similarity and transaction time proximity (within 1 second). It handles potential null values gracefully, ensuring robustness under high load conditions. The function also includes logging for performance analysis and debugging purposes.

The solution is scalable and maintainable, balancing efficiency, usability, and flexibility. External data source integration can be achieved by modifying the `Transaction` class to read data from a database or file. Performance constraints are considered through the use of efficient data structures and algorithms.']

