```

2. Implement a retry mechanism using exponential backoff:

```java
private void retryOperation(Runnable operation, int maxRetries, int initialBackoffMillis, int multiplier) {
    AtomicInteger retries = new AtomicInteger(0);
    Runnable wrappedOperation = () -> {
        if (retries.get() < maxRetries) {
            try {
                operation.run();
            } catch (Exception e) {
                int backoffMillis = initialBackoffMillis * Math.pow(multiplier, retries.get());
                logError("Operation failed, retrying in " + backoffMillis + " milliseconds: " + e.getMessage());
                retries.incrementAndGet();
                try {
                    Thread.sleep(backoffMillis);
                } catch (InterruptedException ignored) {}
                executor.submit(wrappedOperation);
            }
        } else {
            logError("Maximum retries reached for operation: " + e.getMessage());
        }
    };
    executor.submit(wrappedOperation);
}
```

3. Use a distributed logging system like Log4j2 or SLF4J with an appropriate appender to handle logging across different nodes.

