[' Here's a Java implementation using the Disjoint Set Union (Union-Find) data structure and caching mechanism for the given task:

```java
import java.util.*;
import java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;
import java.util.concurrent.TimeUnit;
import java.util.stream.Collectors;

public class EventProcessor {
    private static final int WINDOW_SIZE = 5 * 1000; // 5 seconds in milliseconds
    private static final int ROOT = -1;
    private static final ConcurrentHashMap<Integer, Integer> idMap = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
    private static final ConcurrentHashMap<Integer, Integer> parentMap = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
    private static final ConcurrentHashMap<Set<Integer>, Long> cache = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();

    public void processEvents(List<Integer> events) {
        long startTime = System.nanoTime();
        idMap.clear();
        parentMap.clear();
        for (int event : events) {
            union(event);
        }
        Set<Set<Integer>> disjointPairs = findDisjointSets();
        long endTime = System.nanoTime();
        long processingTime = TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS.convert(endTime - startTime, TimeUnit.NANOSECONDS);
        long count = disjointPairs.stream().mapToLong(set -> cache.getOrDefault(set, countDisjointPairs(set))).sum();
        System.out.printf("Count of disjoint pairs: %d%n", count);
        System.out.printf("Processing time (ms): %d%n", processingTime);
        System.out.printf("Memory usage (MB): %.2f%n", (float) Runtime.getRuntime().totalMemory() / (1024 * 1024));
    }

    private void union(int event) {
        int id = idMap.computeIfAbsent(event, k -> find(k));
        if (id != ROOT) {
            int rootId = find(parentMap.get(id));
            parentMap.put(id, rootId);
        }
    }

    private int find(int event) {
        if (parentMap.get(event) == ROOT) return event;
        return parentMap.put(event, find(parentMap.get(event)));
    }

    private Set<Set<Integer>> findDisjointSets() {
        return idMap.keySet().stream()
                .filter(event -> find(event) == ROOT)
                .collect(Collectors.groupingBy(event -> find(parentMap.get(event)), Collectors.toList()))
                .entrySet().stream()
                .map(entry -> new HashSet<>(entry.getValue()))
                .collect(Collectors.toSet());
    }

    private long countDisjointPairs(Set<Integer> set) {
        Set<Integer> key = new HashSet<>();
        for (int event : set) {
            int id = find(event);
            if (!key.contains(id)) {
                key.add(id);
            }
        }
        return key.size() * (key.size() - 1) / 2;
    }
}
```

This implementation uses a Disjoint Set Union data structure to manage event disjointness dynamically, caching results for repeated computations, and minimizing memory usage while maintaining fast response times. The `processEvents` method takes a list of events as input, processes them in batches, and outputs the count of disjoint pairs, processing time, and memory usage for each window update.']

