        COMPRESSION_FACTORIES.add(new GzipCompressionStreamFactory());
        COMPRESSION_FACTORIES.add(new ZipCompressionStreamFactory());
        COMPRESSION_FACTORIES.add(new ZstdCompressionStreamFactory());
    }

    public static List<LogEntry> processLogFile(byte[] compressedData) {
        try (InputStream input = new ByteArrayInputStream(compressedData)) {
            for (CompressionStreamFactory factory : COMPRESSION_FACTORIES) {
                try (InputStream decompressed = factory.createDecompressor(input)) {
                    return parseLogEntries(decompressed);
                } catch (IOException e) {
                    // Log error and continue with next compression algorithm
                }
            }
            // Return empty list if all decompression attempts fail
            return new ArrayList<>();
        } catch (IOException e) {
            // Handle any I/O errors that occurred during reading the compressed data
        }
    }

    private static List<LogEntry> parseLogEntries(InputStream inputStream) throws IOException {
        List<LogEntry> logEntries = new ArrayList<>();
        BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(inputStream));
        String line;
        while ((line = reader.readLine()) != null) {
            LogEntry logEntry = parseLogEntry(line);
            if (logEntry != null) {
                logEntries.add(logEntry);
            }
        }
        return logEntries;
    }

    private static LogEntry parseLogEntry(String line) {
        // Implement parsing logic for the custom LogEntry object
        // This method should handle different log formats and return a valid LogEntry instance or null if parsing fails
    }
}
```

This example uses the Apache Commons Compress library to support multiple compression algorithms. It processes the compressed data in chunks, minimizing memory usage during decompression. The trade-offs between memory usage, CPU load, and decompression speed for different algorithms may vary depending on the specific implementation details of each algorithm.

The selected compression algorithm is determined automatically based on the available factories. In this example, GZIP, ZIP, and ZSTD are supported out of the box. New compression algorithms can be easily added by creating a new CompressionStreamFactory implementation and adding it to the COMPRESSION_FACTORIES list.

The parseLogEntry method should be implemented according to the specific log format requirements. It's essential to handle different log formats gracefully, returning a valid LogEntry instance or null if parsing fails."]

