[" I will provide a basic implementation using a growable array (vector) with a custom `CellularEventLogEntry` structure, ensuring thread safety through the use of mutexes. The solution also includes functions for adding new entries, retrieving the latest N entries, and clearing the log.

To handle potential concurrent access from multiple threads, I will utilize pthreads (POSIX Threads) library in C. This ensures that critical sections are protected, preventing race conditions.

Here's a simplified version of the code:

```c
#include <pthread.h>
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <time.h>

typedef struct {
    time_t timestamp;
    int cell_identity;
    int signal_strength;
} CellularEventLogEntry;

struct log {
    pthread_mutex_t lock;
    size_t capacity;
    size_t size;
    CellularEventLogEntry* entries;
};

void init_log(struct log* log, size_t initial_capacity) {
    log->capacity = initial_capacity;
    log->size = 0;
    log->entries = malloc(initial_capacity * sizeof(CellularEventLogEntry));
    pthread_mutex_init(&log->lock, NULL);
}

void add_entry(struct log* log, const CellularEventLogEntry* entry) {
    pthread_mutex_lock(&log->lock);

    if (log->size == log->capacity) {
        log->capacity *= 2;
        log->entries = realloc(log->entries, log->capacity * sizeof(CellularEventLogEntry));
    }

    log->entries[log->size++] = *entry;

    pthread_mutex_unlock(&log->lock);
}

void get_latest_entries(const struct log* log, size_t n, CellularEventLogEntry* buffer) {
    pthread_mutex_lock(&log->lock);

    if (log->size < n) {
        n = log->size;
    }

    memcpy(buffer, log->entries + log->size - n, n * sizeof(CellularEventLogEntry));

    pthread_mutex_unlock(&log->lock);
}

void clear_log(struct log* log) {
    pthread_mutex_lock(&log->lock);
    free(log->entries);
    log->size = 0;
    log->capacity = 0;
    pthread_mutex_unlock(&log->lock);
}
```

This implementation uses a growable array (vector) for the dynamic array of `CellularEventLogEntry` structures. The mutex is used to protect critical sections and prevent race conditions when multiple threads access the log concurrently.

The `add_entry()` function handles adding new entries, while the `get_latest_entries()` function retrieves the latest N entries from the log. The `clear_log()` function clears the entire log when requested.

